  "practice": [
    "Find ঁ in চাঁদ, দাঁত, কাঁদা, হাঁটা, and পাঁচ, then read each word aloud without pronouncing ঁ as a separate n or ng.",
    "Compare চাদর (chador, sheet/cover) with চাঁদ (chãd, moon) and let the vowel in চাঁদ resonate slightly through your nose.",
    "Compare বাধা (obstacle) with বাঁধা (tied / to bind) to hear how chandrabindu can affect pronunciation and meaning.",
    "Compare ঁ and ং: ঁ nasalizes a vowel, while ং generally represents a nasal consonant sound like ng.",
    "Use চাঁদ, দাঁত, দাঁড়ানো, কাঁদা, কাঁধ, কাঁটা, কাঁচা, কাঁচি, বাঁশ, বাঁশি, বাঁকা, হাঁটা, হাঁটু, হাঁস, পাঁচ, আঁকা, সাঁতার, ফাঁকা, ঝাঁপ, and ভাঁজ as reading anchors."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঁ is called চন্দ্রবিন্দু (chôndrobindu). It is a mark, not a separate vowel or consonant.",
    "Chandrabindu nasalizes the vowel: some air passes through the nose while the vowel is pronounced. Its shape resembles a tiny moon and dot.",
    "Chandrabindu can affect both pronunciation and meaning, as in বাধা and বাঁধা.",
    "ঁ and ং are different marks: ঁ nasalizes a vowel, while ং (anusvara) generally represents a nasal consonant sound. Compare চাঁদ (chãd, moon) with রং (rong, color).",
    "When reading চাঁদ, দাঁত, কাঁদা, হাঁটা, or পাঁচ, do not pronounce ঁ as a separate n or ng; instead, let the vowel resonate slightly through the nose."
  ]
